184
00:08:26,741 --> 00:08:29,631
And only if we don't find any child elements

185
00:08:29,647 --> 00:08:32,602
anymore that are bigger, only then we know

186
00:08:32,843 --> 00:08:35,171
that the biggest one is at the top. That's

187
00:08:35,171 --> 00:08:36,391
the idea behind this loop.

188
00:08:38,259 --> 00:08:39,945
So therefore, inside of the loop,

189
00:08:41,663 --> 00:08:43,932
I'm going to create a new constant current

190
00:08:43,997 --> 00:08:46,438
node, which is this heap elements

191
00:08:47,858 --> 00:08:48,971
for the current

192
00:08:49,874 --> 00:08:50,778
element index,

193
00:08:51,423 --> 00:08:53,246
because we're again going to swap them.

194
00:08:56,785 --> 00:08:59,158
And we got our current child node, which we

195
00:08:59,158 --> 00:09:01,628
get through this heap elements

196
00:09:02,627 --> 00:09:02,996
for

197
00:09:04,327 --> 00:09:07,373
the child element index. And of course, this

198
00:09:07,373 --> 00:09:09,314
here should also use square brackets

199
00:09:09,939 --> 00:09:11,543
because we're not calling a method here,

200
00:09:11,623 --> 00:09:13,595
we're just accessing a value by index.

201
00:09:14,269 --> 00:09:16,594
And now that we saved those nodes here,

202
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:18,069
we can swap them

203
00:09:18,598 --> 00:09:20,699
and we can set this heap elements

204
00:09:21,469 --> 00:09:23,441
for the child index

205
00:09:24,115 --> 00:09:26,071
equal to the current node

206
00:09:27,161 --> 00:09:28,909
and set heap elements

207
00:09:29,487 --> 00:09:31,045
for the current

208
00:09:32,137 --> 00:09:35,316
element index equal to the child, the

209
00:09:35,364 --> 00:09:36,616
current child node.

210
00:09:37,917 --> 00:09:39,924
So we're again swapping that. And since

211
00:09:39,924 --> 00:09:41,433
we're doing this in a loop, we'll then

212
00:09:41,449 --> 00:09:44,821
compare the swapped new top value with its

213
00:09:44,821 --> 00:09:45,656
child values.

214
00:09:46,604 --> 00:09:49,060
And after this loop completed, we'll again

215
00:09:49,092 --> 00:09:51,677
have a heap where the biggest value is at

216
00:09:51,677 --> 00:09:52,143
the top.

217
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:55,339
Let's see whether that works. At the moment,

218
00:09:55,419 --> 00:09:58,601
250 is at the top. So if we call

219
00:09:59,517 --> 00:10:01,413
heap_process here,

220
00:10:02,409 --> 00:10:06,418
we should see that this is removed and 197

221
00:10:06,676 --> 00:10:08,175
should thereafter be at the top.

222
00:10:09,892 --> 00:10:12,545
If I reload, I get an error that heap is not

