233
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:40,765
And I know that this logic with that

234
00:10:40,895 --> 00:10:44,162
swapping and that while loop can be tricky

235
00:10:44,195 --> 00:10:46,783
to wrap your head around, but I hope that I

236
00:10:46,783 --> 00:10:48,644
could still explain this in an

237
00:10:48,828 --> 00:10:50,396
understandable way what we're doing.

238
00:10:51,438 --> 00:10:52,465
For inserting,

239
00:10:53,059 --> 00:10:55,676
we're inserting data at the end and then

240
00:10:55,709 --> 00:10:58,342
we're comparing it to its various parent

241
00:10:58,342 --> 00:11:00,863
nodes to move it up in the tree.

242
00:11:01,714 --> 00:11:04,026
And for removing, for processing,

243
00:11:04,684 --> 00:11:06,370
we're in the end doing the opposite.

244
00:11:07,012 --> 00:11:09,292
We're removing the topmost element because

245
00:11:09,357 --> 00:11:11,685
that always is the element we wanna process.

246
00:11:12,472 --> 00:11:14,366
And then we wanna ensure that the new

247
00:11:14,575 --> 00:11:17,417
biggest element moves to the top. Therefore,

248
00:11:17,546 --> 00:11:20,484
we take a random element and start comparing

249
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:22,090
it to its child nodes.

250
00:11:22,684 --> 00:11:24,610
And if we find a bigger one there, we use

251
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:25,831
the bigger one as the new

252
00:11:26,457 --> 00:11:28,817
top node and we start comparing that.

253
00:11:29,492 --> 00:11:32,799
And we keep on doing that until we find no

254
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:34,293
